R82: an element inside a library section or an `if` branch, altered by name from the top level.
ngspice-45 -b and vacask, `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/scope/run.sh` (light lane). The divider r1 = 1k over r2 = 1k
gives v(b) = 0.5; after `alter r2 3k` / `alter instance("r2") r=3k` it gives 0.75.
Rechecked 2026-11-13 under R91b (../checked.sh: a run whose exit status is not 0 or whose output says it aborted, stepped too small or met a singular matrix gives refused(<why>), never a reading): every reading reproduced, none refused.

ngspice section.cir:  v(b) = 5.000000e-01   then   v(b) = 7.500000e-01
ngspice if.cir:       v(b) = 5.000000e-01   then   v(b) = 7.500000e-01
vacask section.sim:   op1 b = 5.000000000000000e-01   op2 b = 7.500000000000000e-01
vacask if.sim:        op1 b = 5.000000000000000e-01   op2 b = 7.500000000000000e-01
(if.cir and if.sim hold an `r2` in each branch; the alter reaches the one the condition keeps.)
